  "source_facts": {
    "producer": "4ffe10 local case80 and43e610 remote case80 set body+2c=3, normalize parameter1 into body+2a8 and clear auxiliary+3c counter. They do not write normal f536a0/remote record resource, change facing, clear motion or consume parameter2.",
    "spin": "439080 case3 counters0..360 inclusive set action3, save initial body facing at counter0 and derive the rotating facing from initialFacing-trunc(((360-counter+8)%120)/15), with source signed remainder8. Base projected screen coordinates use source+0.5 then truncation. Geometry uses raw source single/double constants at52d908..52d927, independently byte checked.",
    "finish": "For counter>360, first call4fd0d0(action4,speed100,mode1,staticFlip0). Only return1 resets body specialState0/counter0/action0; then always call4fd0d0 again with mode0 and current action. Counter increments afterward, so successful finish retains counter1. Static/frozen return0 is not a fabricated completion.",
    "draw": "439080 returns1 after its own462cc0 root and causes43ba10 to exit before ordinary motion, range/dedup and local queue flag1. Spin root has default sortFlag0 even for local; logical depth coordinates remain the actual actor position, screen offsets alone change.",
    "local_sources": "Local case60 updates normal f536a0;80 changes only body. Normal local source globals and temporary body resource/facing must not be conflated during ready scene reconstruction or unit refresh. Local461660 movement and4ff5a0 position/velocity synchronization continue independently of the special callback; facing assignment must follow real source movement/turn writes rather than copy the special body's rotated facing back to its normal source. After completion the body keeps its final spin facing until an actual facing writer; normal globals are not copied into it on every idle frame.462410 compares requested direction against actual body+2b8, even when the normal source already equals that direction.",
    "boundary": "43ba10 remains outside the provider's procedure body; use retained exact callback disassembly. State1/2, ride/child rendering and unobserved gates remain explicit and unfinished. No target execution is inferred from static bytes.",
    "local_dispatch_guard": "4f2010 at4f2176 reads current body+2a8 and skips local action dispatch when that body resource is0. Keep this actual body guard; separating normal globals must not mechanically replace every body read with a normal-resource read."
  },
